#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-rockblock.rst:105
#: 1b015c94dccf44e482b06c8cfc9a9e0b
msgid "Data is prepaid on a per-byte basis. Each ``HIGH_LATENCY2`` message sent or received is 52 bytes. So, for example, if the RockBLOCK was configured to send 1 ``HIGH_LATENCY2`` message every 30 seconds that would give a data usage of 6.24 KB per hour. If any commands are sent from the GCS to the vehicle via the RockBLOCK, they should be added too. For example, if 5 commands are sent in the same hour, that is an additional 220 bytes. Combining both sent and received messages, a total of 6.46 KB per hour are used."
msgstr ""

